1. She struggled with sleep and likely only got around 3–4 hours. (Verbatim: "I think I had, how many, I remember, I checked the time when I was trying to sleep. I kept like half waking up and I think it was like three something, yeah.")

2. She enjoys cereal and apple juice for breakfast. (Verbatim: "I didn't even have a big bowl of cereal. I had a small bowl... I have here, apple juice, cartons.")

3. She finds it difficult to relax her mind and stop thinking when trying to sleep. (Verbatim: "how does one not think... my brain is like that's it my brain go I don't know how")

4. She once tried a brainwave-relaxation device during a school computer tech trip. (Verbatim: "I was on like a computer tech trip and there was like a machine with this ball and this little thing that you put around your head... designed to help students like relax")

5. She dislikes being told to exercise as a solution to everything. (Verbatim: "why is exercise always the answer why is the answer never curl up in bed and eat chicken burger")

6. She discovered she enjoys salad when it has dressing, unlike when she ate it plain as a child. (Verbatim: "everyone had these yummy dressings and i was eating my salad with with nothing so salad only taste like the dressing")

7. She had a very enjoyable trip to Japan, especially in Akihabara. (Verbatim: "i had the bestest time i had so much fun i had a lot a lot a lot a lot a lot of fun")

8. She wants to improve her Japanese language skills for her next trip to Japan. (Verbatim: "next time i go to japan though i want to be able to speak japan japan better i want to be able to speak japanese better")

9. She has a strong fondness for crème brûlée. (Verbatim: "i love creme brulee i love i love i love creme brulee")

10. She associates comfort and sleep with fantasizing or letting her mind wander into stories. (Verbatim: "personally i fall asleep by having someone that i can comfortable let my mind spin around such as fantasy stories") [end of text]



1. She previously worked at a zoo, caring for various animals including rhinos, giraffes, lemurs, and tortoises. (Verbatim: "worked so um where i worked there were two rhinos... i looked after a giraffe family... i looked after lemurs... i looked after tortoise")

2. She had to separate a female rhino from the male on days when she was in an annoyed mood. (Verbatim: "the female rhino would be in too much of like an annoyed mood... i always had to separate them on grumpy days")

3. She found cleaning up rhino poop to be one of the most time-consuming and unpleasant parts of her zoo job. (Verbatim: "rhinos definitely had the biggest largest amount of poop i had to pick up... it was stupid how much there was")

4. She disliked cleaning the indoor lemur enclosure because one lemur habitually threw its poop onto the radiator. (Verbatim: "one of the lemurs kept throwing its poop on the radiator... that's gross because it's literally on a heater")

5. She had to wear face protection when handling an aggressive female lemur who tried to mate with her offspring. (Verbatim: "you had to wear proper face helmet gear because she was so angy and frustrated")

6. She cared for leopard tortoises and had to play hide-and-seek to find them at the end of the day. (Verbatim: "i looked after leopard tortoises... you had to play hide and seek with these at the end of the day and go look for them all")

7. She knows the proper way to hold a tortoise, using two hands to support it gently underneath. (Verbatim: "you should hold them very gently like always hold them with like two hands and give them support underneath")

8. She considered getting a tortoise as a pet but was deterred by their long lifespan, noting they could outlive her. (Verbatim: "i was kind of close to getting a tortoise once but it would like outlive me right i think")

9. She finds rhinos cute despite their danger, noting their small human-sized tongues and lazy morning behavior. (Verbatim: "rhinos are really cute animals minus their absolute danger... they're also very lazy and they don't like to wake up in the morning")

10. She finds giraffe pee to have the worst smell, particularly due to its strong ammonia odor. (Verbatim: "the smelliest thing was the giraffe... giraffe pee it was very strong like ammonia smell to it") [end of text]



